NAME
     curl - fetch a URL

SYNOPSIS
     curl [-s] [-i] [-I] [-L] [-f] [-o FILE] [-O] [-X METHOD]
          [-H HEADER] [-d DATA] URL

DESCRIPTION
     curl fetches a URL over HTTP and writes the body to standard
     output.

OPTIONS
     -s          silent: no progress
     -i          print the headers too
     -I          the headers only (a HEAD request)
     -L          follow redirects
     -f          fail quietly on an error status
     -o FILE     write the body there
     -O          write it to the file the URL names
     -X METHOD   use this method
     -H HEADER   add a header
     -d DATA     send DATA as the body (and POST by default)

SEE ALSO
     wget(1), https(1), nc(1)
